    <p>The common thread across all four professions: the metadata that creates the most risk is rarely the metadata you chose to include. It's the metadata your software, your document management system, or your operating system added without asking. Understanding which fields carry that automatic data — and building a verification step into your document workflow — is what separates professionals who manage this risk from those who discover it too late.</p>

    <p>For a complete reference to every PDF metadata field and what each one contains, see our <a href="/blog/pdf-metadata-fields-explained">PDF metadata fields explained</a> guide. For the technical removal workflow, see <a href="/blog/remove-metadata-from-pdf">how to remove metadata from a PDF</a>.</p>

